### Span - Example

If $A = \{e_1, e_2, e_3\}$ consists  of the *canonical basis vectors* of $\mathbb R ^3$, that is

$$
e_1 :=
\begin{bmatrix}
     1 \\
     0 \\
     0
\end{bmatrix}
, \quad
e_2 :=
\begin{bmatrix}
     0 \\
     1 \\
     0
\end{bmatrix}
, \quad
e_3 :=
\begin{bmatrix}
     0 \\
     0 \\
     1
\end{bmatrix}
$$

then the span of $A$ is all of $\mathbb R ^3$, because, for any $x = (x_1, x_2, x_3) \in \mathbb R ^3$, we can write

$$
x = x_1 e_1 + x_2 e_2 + x_3 e_3
$$

